; CActor-derived peer avatar (class CXrrPeerAvatar). Inherits the full [actor]
; parameter set (camera, conditions, immunities, damage) — the class reads them
; exactly like the real player. script_binding = deliberate no-op:
; bind_stalker.actor_init on a second actor would clobber db.actor, and an
; empty value feeds "" to CScriptBinder's functor lookup (error per spawn).
; character_profile actor_stalker puts every avatar in one community;
; per-faction variants are a relations concern, still open.
[xrr_avatar]:actor
class             = XRRAVATR
script_binding    = xrr_core.bind_avatar
character_profile = actor_stalker

; ── Squad-registry map beacon ────────────────────────────────────────────────
; Inert offline se-object the peer materializes for a same-level, policy-passing
; squad that has NO commander mirror (the squad is off every player's bubble).
; SQUAD_REGISTRY MOVE deltas keep its graph position fresh, and unmodified
; CMapLocation machinery renders the squad-leader spot from it — exactly as
; vanilla renders an offline squad's spot from the commander's se-object.
;
; Inherits space_restrictor (class SPC_RS_S = no visual, no AI, no physics
; collision). The peer pins it in C++ (xrr_squad_sync.cpp ensure_beacon):
; can_switch_online(false) so it never onlines / never runs bind_restrictor,
; and flCanSave=FALSE so it never enters a peer save — it is re-derived from the
; registry every session and dies with the level's a-life on a transition.
[xrr_squad_beacon]:space_restrictor
